{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015GmpETtJcwUFzAwnpiYybj","type":"tool_result","content":"90\t_BOOTSTRAP_REGISTRY_SHA256: Optional[str] = None  # placeholder pre-GENESIS\n91\t\n92\t# PLAN-045 Wave 1 P0-01 — signer allowlist for sentinel .asc signatures.\n93\t_SENTINEL_SIGNERS_FILE = (\n94\t    Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent.parent\n95\t    / \".claude\" / \"sentinel-signers.txt\"\n96\t)\n97\t\n98\t\n99\t# Canonical paths (relative to repo root) — ADR-010 v1.1 (Sprint 9\n100\t# amendment adds conftest.py + new-hook + lessons-related scripts).\n101\t# fnmatch.fnmatch is used; `*` is treated as a single segment matcher\n102\t# below by walking the path components manually. `**` matches zero or\n103\t# more segments (used for the Sprint 9 conftest entry).\n104\t#\n105\t# PLAN-019 Phase 2 Wave 2A (P1-SEC-A) expansion: full governance surface.\n106\t# Every path listed here is sentinel-gated (editable via Owner-signed\n107\t# sentinel). The arbitration-kernel subset (hook source files enforcing\n108\t# THIS guard, _lib/policy.py, _lib/redact.py, _lib/audit_emit.py, and\n109\t# .claude/policies/*.yaml) is ALSO covered by the stricter HARD-DENY\n110\t# hook `check_arbitration_kernel.py` — that hook has no sentinel escape\n111\t# and requires `CEO_KERNEL_OVERRIDE` with an audit-logged reason. The\n112\t# overlap is intentional defense-in-depth: if the arbitration hook is\n113\t# disabled by misconfiguration, this sentinel guard still blocks the\n114\t# edits (and vice versa).\n115\t# Canonical governance surfaces: `.claude/skills/**/SKILL.md` and\n116\t# `.claude/commands/**` stay sentinel-guarded. These tokens are also the\n117\t# command/skill-hook map generator's source-scanning contract.\n118\ttry:\n119\t    from _lib.canonical_edit import guards as _canonical_guard_definitions\n120\t    for _guard_name in _canonical_guard_definitions.__all__:\n121\t        globals()[_guard_name] = getattr(_canonical_guard_definitions, _guard_name)\n122\t    del _guard_name, _canonical_guard_definitions\n123\texcept Exception:\n124\t    _CANONICAL_GUARDS = []\n125\t    _SKILL_CONTENT_RE = re.compile(r\"^$\")\n126\t    _SKILL_LOADED_RE = re.compile(r\"^$\")\n127\t    _VALID_BLOCKED_TOOLS = frozenset()\n128\t\n129\t# Set ONCE per invocation by ``main()`` from the parsed event, and reset\n130\t# in its ``finally`` so a value can never leak into a later in-process\n131\t# caller. Helpers deep in the call graph (``_emit_unlock_audit`` has no\n132\t# event in scope) read it through ``_blocked_tool_field()``.\n133\t_CURRENT_TOOL_NAME = \"\"\n134\t\n135\t\n136\t# Blocked-tool validation and skill-content checks are bound below.\n137\t\n138\t\n139\t# PLAN-025 F-perf-004 fast-path — precomputed set of top-level path\n140\t# segments that every _CANONICAL_GUARDS entry starts with. Any path NOT\n141\t# starting with one of these prefixes is non-canonical in O(1) without\n142\t# running fnmatch 30+ times. Preserves semantics — every guard pattern\n143\t# starts with one of these prefixes by construction.\n144\t_CANONICAL_PREFIXES = frozenset({\n145\t    \".claude\", \".github\", \"scripts\", \"SPEC\", \"PROTOCOL.md\",\n146\t    # PLAN-155 Wave 3b (SENT-CX-E) — first-segment prefixes for the Codex\n147\t    # kill-switch surface. Without these three the fast-path bail-out in\n148\t    # `_is_canonical` returns False BEFORE the new `_CANONICAL_GUARDS`\n149\t    # entries are ever consulted (the guard would be dead — the S254\n150\t    # dead-gate class). Every kill-switch guard pattern starts with one of\n151\t    # these by construction (`.codex/*`, `requirements.toml`, `AGENTS.md`).\n152\t    \".codex\", \"requirements.toml\", \"AGENTS.md\",\n153\t    # PLAN-156 Wave 3 (SENT-GK-E) — the same dead-guard class as `.codex`\n154\t    # above, twice over (pair-rail R4 + R14). `_is_canonical()` bails out\n155\t    # BEFORE any glob matching unless the path's first segment is in this\n156\t    # set, so adding the `.grok/**` and `templates/settings/*` patterns to\n157\t    # _CANONICAL_GUARDS without adding their first segments HERE would\n158\t    # leave both guards INERT — unsentineled edits sailing straight through\n159\t    # a list that LOOKS like it protects them. The S254 dead-gate class,\n160\t    # and the reason this pair of edits can never be split across waves.\n161\t    \".grok\", \"templates\",\n162\t})\n163\t\n164\t\n165\t# PLAN160_FIX_A / PLAN160_FIX_C / PLAN160_FIX_D — upper bound on candidates\n166\t# classified per multi-candidate event, resolve-fault fail-closed in decide(),\n167\t# and relative-path canonical resolution against repo_root.\n168\t# event. Beyond this the event is fail-CLOSED (blocked) rather than risk an\n169\t# unexamined canonical candidate riding through past a truncated scan. Real\n170\t# apply_patch / MCP bulk events carry a handful of paths; this is a DoS-shape\n171\t# backstop, not a normal-path limit.\n172\t_PLAN160_MAX_CANDIDATES = 512\n173\t\n174\t\n175\t# PLAN162_FIX_CASEFOLD (PLAN-162 consensus S1, P0 — BOTH rails).\n176\t#\n177\t# ``_match_segments`` matches with ``fnmatch.fnmatchcase`` (exact case)\n178\t# and ``_CANONICAL_PREFIXES`` is an exact-case frozenset. On a\n179\t# case-INSENSITIVE filesystem — APFS, the default on this repo's\n180\t# platform — ``.claude/settings.JSON`` IS ``.claude/settings.json``, and\n181\t# writing through the variant OVERWRITES the guarded file. Measured on\n182\t# HEAD: `.claude/settings.JSON`, `.claude/hooks/_lib/audit_emit.PY` and\n183\t# `.CLAUDE/settings.json` all classified NON-canonical AND non-kernel,\n184\t# reaching files the threat model assumes unreachable.\n185\t#\n186\t# Both halves must fold or the guard only LOOKS fixed: the prefix\n187\t# fast-path bails out in O(1) BEFORE any glob runs, so folding the glob\n188\t# matcher alone would leave `.CLAUDE/...` inert — the dead-gate class\n189\t# this file was already bitten by twice (the `.codex` and `.grok` prefix\n190\t# omissions).\n191\t#\n192\t# ``str.lower`` — not ``str.casefold`` — deliberately: casefold expands\n193\t# 'ß'→'ss', changing segment LENGTH and hence what a glob matches. The\n194\t# exploited class is ASCII case variance, which ``lower()`` covers\n195\t# exactly; identical inputs always fold identically, so the\n196\t# normalization can only ADD matches (over-classify = the safe\n197\t# direction), never remove one.\n198\t#\n199\t# Precomputed at import: the hot path pays one ``str.lower()`` per\n200\t# classification instead of one per (segment x pattern).\n201\t_CANONICAL_GUARDS_FOLDED = [pat.lower() for pat in _CANONICAL_GUARDS]\n202\t_CANONICAL_PREFIXES_FOLDED = frozenset(\n203\t    prefix.lower() for prefix in _CANONICAL_PREFIXES\n204\t)\n205\t\n206\t\n207\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n208\t# PLAN162_FIX_2: depth-independent discovery now lives in canonical_edit.paths.\n209\t# PLAN-094 Wave C — sentinel verification session cache (R-041)\n210\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n211\t# Module-scope ONLY (NEVER file-backed; PLAN-094 §3 Wave C C.1).\n212\t# Process death = cache loss (eliminates R5 stale-cache-survives-crash).\n213\t# Composite key — Codex iter-1 P0 fold: target_rel included so cache value\n214\t# (grant decision dependent on target_rel) is correct on hit; sha256_full\n215\t# transitively covers signer changes via .asc bytes (signer rotation\n216\t# window risk acknowledged + accepted trade-off per design draft §8).\n217\t\n218\t_SENTINEL_CACHE_FORMAT_VERSION = 2  # bumped at iter-1 P0 fix (target_rel added)\n219\t_SENTINEL_VERIFY_CACHE: Dict["}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"15f68acd-8563-46de-ac1c-c65891f7fb4e","uuid":"90ae3876-9584-4aa1-bced-aab115b3b1a4","timestamp":"2026-11-16T18:05:03.920Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.n5R3O9/tree/.claude/hooks/check_canoni