{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KxHRKyctoF8e56jwg3cLXX","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t{\n2\t  \"_comment\": \"CEO Orchestration — local settings for THIS repo (ceo-orchestration itself). Source of truth for distribution lives in templates/settings/ (settings.base.json + settings.stack.<name>.json). This file is a dogfooded BASE install — no tsc/vitest pre-commit gate because this repo has no TypeScript.\",\n3\t  \"_squad_allowlist_comment\": \"Sprint 11 CR2: empty default means nothing imports. Owners add entries via git; see ADR-039 + docs/squad-marketplace.md.\",\n4\t  \"squad_allowlist\": [],\n5\t  \"_sandbox_comment\": \"PLAN-136 W3 S4b: OS-level Bash containment composed into the LIVE dogfood install (no longer SPOF fail-open — the env-layer sandbox sits UNDER the hook rail and does NOT fail open). Values copied from templates/settings/settings.stack.sandbox.json (PLAN-135 W2 / S4). enabled=true contains each Bash tool-call; allowUnixSockets keeps local IPC (audit filelock, git local sockets); filesystem.writablePaths scopes writes to the repo tree + scratch ($CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR, /tmp, /var/folders), HOME stays non-writable (startup-file class); network.defaultPosture=deny with allowedDomains = the PLAN-133 egress SoT (_lib/egress_taxonomy.py _PAIR_RAIL_HOST_SUFFIXES) + operationally-required hosts. autoAllowBashIfSandboxed SHIPPED FALSE (a fail-open hook + auto-allow makes allowedDomains the SOLE exfil control — deliberate adopter choice only).\",\n6\t  \"sandbox\": {\n7\t    \"_comment\": \"OS-level containment for Bash tool-calls. SHIPPED enabled:false (Codex R1 P1) — the sandbox config is composed-and-ready in the live install, but NOT active until you flip enabled:true AFTER a sandbox probe (curl/gh/pip/npm/codex/anthropic) confirms allowedDomains covers your real workflows. When enabled, the harness runs each Bash command inside it; allowUnix keeps local IPC working (audit filelock, git local sockets); network.allowedDomains is the egress allowlist; default posture is deny.\",\n8\t    \"enabled\": false,\n9\t    \"allowUnixSockets\": true,\n10\t    \"filesystem\": {\n11\t      \"_disabled_comment\": \"PLAN-163 T1/OQ5(c) — CC 2.1.220 sandbox.filesystem.disabled evaluated against the real dogfood flows (ceremony scripts, review_loop git-init, eval scratch runs all operate inside writablePaths + /tmp): DECISION = keep filesystem confinement ARMED (disabled:false, explicit). Setting true would fail-OPEN the FS layer while keeping network containment — rejected; revisit only with a named flow that writablePaths cannot express. Rollback: flip this key to true (single-line revert), no other key depends on it.\",\n12\t      \"disabled\": false,\n13\t      \"_comment\": \"Paths the sandboxed Bash process may read/write. repo = the project tree (so Edit/Write/build/test all work); /tmp = scratch (mktemp scratch dirs used by review_loop.py git-init, eval/probe scratch runs, hermetic venvs). HOME is NOT writable: keeps a sandboxed command from rewriting ~/.bashrc / ~/.claude profile/credential files (harvest D5 startup-file class). $CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR expands to the repo root at install time.\",\n14\t      \"writablePaths\": [\n15\t        \"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR\",\n16\t        \"/tmp\",\n17\t        \"/var/folders\"\n18\t      ],\n19\t      \"readablePaths\": [\n20\t        \"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR\",\n21\t        \"/tmp\",\n22\t        \"/usr\",\n23\t        \"/bin\",\n24\t        \"/opt\"\n25\t      ]\n26\t    },\n27\t    \"network\": {\n28\t      \"_comment\": \"allowedDomains = PLAN-133 egress allowlist (see _network_allowlist_comment). Default posture is DENY: a host not on this list is unreachable from a sandboxed Bash command, which is the ~84%-fewer-prompts containment that retires the regex whack-a-mole (5 env(1) bypasses found in S223). deniedDomains is an explicit carve-back layer, empty by design.\",\n29\t      \"defaultPosture\": \"deny\",\n30\t      \"strictAllowlist\": true,\n31\t      \"allowedDomains\": [\n32\t        \"openai.com\",\n33\t        \"api.openai.com\",\n34\t        \"githubcopilot.com\",\n35\t        \"codex.dev\",\n36\t        \"anthropic.com\",\n37\t        \"api.anthropic.com\",\n38\t        \"github.com\",\n39\t        \"api.github.com\",\n40\t        \"raw.githubusercontent.com\",\n41\t        \"objects.githubusercontent.com\",\n42\t        \"codeload.github.com\",\n43\t        \"registry.npmjs.org\",\n44\t        \"pypi.org\",\n45\t        \"files.pythonhosted.org\",\n46\t        \"api.osv.dev\"\n47\t      ],\n48\t      \"deniedDomains\": []\n49\t    },\n50\t    \"_credentials_comment\": \"PLAN-153 wave-backlog (Anthropic ADOPT sweep 2026-07) — Claude Code >=2.1.187 sandbox.credentials, schema verified against the 2.1.202 binary (files[].mode is literal 'deny'; envVars[].mode is 'deny'|'mask'; allowPlaintextInject optional, defaults false). Denies sandboxed Bash commands access to credential FILES (the subprocess-read class the permissions.deny Read() rail explicitly cannot cover — see _deny_baseline_comment) and unsets secret ENV VARS for sandboxed commands. INERT until sandbox.enabled=true (same flip discipline as the rest of this block). Honest limits: (1) this rail is HARNESS-side fail-open — the 2.1.202 loader drops an invalid entry or the whole block with a warning ('no credential protection is applied until it is fixed'), so the hook-side fail-CLOSED credential-leak guard in check_bash_safety.py remains the primary rail and this is defense-in-depth; (2) files paths resolve like sandbox.filesystem.* (absolute, ~ expanded, or relative to the project root) with NO glob support — the .env entries cover the repo ROOT only; subdir dotenv reads stay owned by the Read() deny rail + contamination CI; (3) envVars deliberately EXCLUDES GH_TOKEN/GITHUB_TOKEN/ANTHROPIC_API_KEY/OPENAI_API_KEY because gh, the `claude -p` eval harnesses, and the codex pair-rail all run through sandboxed Bash and may legitimately consume them — tighten only after an Owner-run probe (WATCH in docs/substrate-adopt-2026-07.md); (4) 'mask' mode (sentinel-in-sandbox + proxy inject on egress) is deliberately unused: it rests on egress-proxy TLS assumptions we have not probed; allowPlaintextInject stays explicit false.\",\n51\t    \"credentials\": {\n52\t      \"files\": [\n53\t        {\n54\t          \"path\": \"~/.ssh\",\n55\t          \"mode\": \"deny\"\n56\t        },\n57\t        {\n58\t          \"path\": \"~/.aws\",\n59\t          \"mode\": \"deny\"\n60\t        },\n61\t        {\n62\t          \"path\": \"~/.npmrc\",\n63\t          \"mode\": \"deny\"\n64\t        },\n65\t        {\n66\t          \"path\": \"~/.config/gcloud\",\n67\t          \"mode\": \"deny\"\n68\t        },\n69\t        {\n70\t          \"path\": \"~/.kube\",\n71\t          \"mode\": \"deny\"\n72\t        },\n73\t        {\n74\t          \"path\": \"~/.docker/config.json\",\n75\t          \"mode\": \"deny\"\n76\t        },\n77\t        {\n78\t          \"path\": \"~/.git-credentials\",\n79\t          \"mode\": \"deny\"\n80\t        },\n81\t        {\n82\t          \"path\": \"~/.netrc\",\n83\t          \"mode\": \"deny\"\n84\t        },\n85\t        {\n86\t          \"path\": \"~/.pypirc\",\n87\t          \"mode\": \"deny\"\n88\t        },\n89\t        {\n90\t          \"path\": \"~/.gnupg\",\n91\t          \"mode\": \"deny\"\n92\t        },\n93\t        {\n94\t          \"path\": \"~/.claude/.credentials.json\",\n95\t          \"mode\": \"deny\"\n96\t        },\n97\t        {\n98\t          \"path\": \".env\",\n99\t          \"mode\": \"deny\"\n100\t        },\n101\t        {\n102\t          \"path\": \".env.local\",\n103\t          \"mode\": \"deny\"\n104\t        }\n105\t      ],\n106\t      \"envVars\": [\n107\t        {\n108\t          \"name\": \"AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID\",\n109\t          \"mode\": \"deny\"\n110\t        },\n111\t        {\n112\t          \"name\": \"AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY\",\n113\t          \"mode\": \"deny\"\n114\t        },\n115\t        {\n116\t          \"name\": \"AWS_SESSION_TOKEN\",\n117\t          \"mode\": \"deny\"\n118\t        },\n119\t        {\n120\t          \"name\": \"NPM_TOKEN\",\n121\t          \"mode\": \"deny\"\n122\t        },\n123\t        {\n124\t          \"name\": \"NODE_AUTH_TOKEN\",\n125\t          \"mode\": \"deny\"\n126\t        }\n127\t      ],\n128\t      \"allowPlaintextInject\": false\n129\t    }\n130\t  },\n131\t  \"autoAllowBashIfSandboxed\": false,\n132\t  \"hooks\": {\n133\t    \"PreToolUse\": [\n134\t      {\n135\t        \"_comment\": \"CORE protocol enforcement: blocks named-agent spawns without ## SKILL CONTENT. Python hook via shim (resolves Python >= 3.9).\",\n136\t        \"matcher\": \"Agent\",\n137\t        \"hooks\": [\n138\t          {\n139\t            \"type\": \"command\",\n140\t            \"command\": \"bash \\\"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/.claude/hooks/_python-hook.sh\\\" check_agent_spawn.py\",\n141\t            \"timeout\": 5,\n142\t            \"statusMessage\": \"Checking agent spawn governance...\"\n143\t          }\n144\t        ]\n145\t      },\n146\t      {\n147\t        \"_comment\": \"Bash safety: shlex-based parser replaces 5 substring-matching rules that false-positived on quoted strings during Sprint 2. Blocks: rm -rf (all flag combos), git reset --hard, git push --force/-f. Allows: --force-with-lease, quoted strings, compound commands with safe clauses. See check_bash_safety.py docstring for full logic.\",\n148\t        \"matcher\": \"Bash\",\n149\t        \"hooks\": [\n150\t          {\n151\t            \"type\": \"command\",\n152\t            \"command\": \"bash \\\"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/.claude/hooks/_python-hook.sh\\\" check_bash_safety.py\",\n153\t            \"timeout\": 5,\n154\t            \"statusMessage\": \"Checking bash safety...\"\n155\t          }\n156\t        ]\n157\t      },\n158\t      {\n159\t        \"_comment\": \"PLAN-133 E1 (Goose-harvest) — adversary local-rules deny/ask gate. DETERMINISTIC local-rules scan over the Bash command, reading patterns from .claude/adversary.md (UNTRUSTED DATA, size-capped, read only INSIDE CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR). LOCAL-RULES-ONLY: NO model call on the hot path (the rite rejected sync Codex here — a measured 40x-600x p99 regression vs the ~5ms warm floor; real adversarial depth lives in the canonical/L3 Codex pair-rail). Default-OFF behaviorally: advisory (emit-only, ALLOW) until CEO_ADVERSARY=1 flips a deny/ask rule to BLOCK. Secret-in-command → fail-CLOSED (deny/flag, never transmit — E1 sends nothing, local-only). Fail-OPEN on any infra error. Own ADR (ADR-146) lands FIRST. Mirror in BOTH this template and .claude/settings.json or test_template_dogfood_parity reddens.\",\n160\t        \"matcher\": \"Bash\","}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"15f68acd-8563-46de-ac1c-c65891f7fb4e","uuid":"6c5609d6-6319-414f-abad-ca2de4baaf98","timestamp":"2026-11-16T18:09:41.191Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.n5R3O9/tree/.claude/settings.json","content":"{\n  \"_comment\": \"CEO Orchestration — local settings for THIS repo (ceo-orchestration itself). Source of truth for distribution lives in templates/settings/ (settings.base.json + settings.stack.<name>.json). This file is a dogfooded BASE install — no tsc/vitest pre-commit gate because this repo has no TypeScript.\",\n  \"_squad_allowlist_comment\": \"Sprint 11 CR2: empty default means nothing imports. Owners add entries via git; see ADR-039 + docs/squad-marketplace.md.\",\n  \"squad_allowlist\": [],\n  \"_sandbox_comment\": \"PLAN-136 W3 S4b: OS-level Bash containment composed into the LIVE dogfood install (no longer SPOF fail-open — the env-layer sandbox sits UNDER the hook rail and does NOT fail open). Values copied from templates/settings/settings.stack.sandbox.json (PLAN-135 W2 / S4). enabled=true contains each Bash tool-call; allowUnixSockets keeps local IPC (audit filelock, git