est limits: (1) this rail is HARNESS-side fail-open — the 2.1.202 loader drops an invalid entry or the whole block with a warning ('no credential protection is applied until it is fixed'), so the hook-side fail-CLOSED credential-leak guard in check_bash_safety.py remains the primary rail and this is defense-in-depth; (2) files paths resolve like sandbox.filesystem.* (absolute, ~ expanded, or relative to the project root) with NO glob support — the .env entries cover the repo ROOT only; subdir dotenv reads stay owned by the Read() deny rail + contamination CI; (3) envVars deliberately EXCLUDES GH_TOKEN/GITHUB_TOKEN/ANTHROPIC_API_KEY/OPENAI_API_KEY because gh, the `claude -p` eval harnesses, and the codex pair-rail all run through sandboxed Bash and may legitimately consume them — tighten only after an Owner-run probe (WATCH in docs/substrate-adopt-2026-07.md); (4) 'mask' mode (sentinel-in-sandbox + proxy inject on egress) is deliberately unused: it rests on egress-proxy TLS assumptions we have not probed; allowPlaintextInject stays explicit false.\",\n    \"credentials\": {\n      \"files\": [\n        {\n          \"path\": \"~/.ssh\",\n          \"mode\": \"deny\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"path\": \"~/.aws\",\n          \"mode\": \"deny\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"path\": \"~/.npmrc\",\n          \"mode\": \"deny\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"path\": \"~/.config/gcloud\",\n          \"mode\": \"deny\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"path\": \"~/.kube\",\n          \"mode\": \"deny\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"path\": \"~/.docker/config.json\",\n          \"mode\": \"deny\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"path\": \"~/.git-credentials\",\n          \"mode\": \"deny\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"path\": \"~/.netrc\",\n          \"mode\": \"deny\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"path\": \"~/.pypirc\",\n          \"mode\": \"deny\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"path\": \"~/.gnupg\",\n          \"mode\": \"de