oks/_python-hook.sh\\\" check_bash_safety.py\",\n            \"timeout\": 5,\n            \"statusMessage\": \"Checking bash safety...\"\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"_comment\": \"PLAN-133 E1 (Goose-harvest) — adversary local-rules deny/ask gate. DETERMINISTIC local-rules scan over the Bash command, reading patterns from .claude/adversary.md (UNTRUSTED DATA, size-capped, read only INSIDE CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR). LOCAL-RULES-ONLY: NO model call on the hot path (the rite rejected sync Codex here — a measured 40x-600x p99 regression vs the ~5ms warm floor; real adversarial depth lives in the canonical/L3 Codex pair-rail). Default-OFF behaviorally: advisory (emit-only, ALLOW) until CEO_ADVERSARY=1 flips a deny/ask rule to BLOCK. Secret-in-command → fail-CLOSED (deny/flag, never transmit — E1 sends nothing, local-only). Fail-OPEN on any infra error. Own ADR (ADR-146) lands FIRST. Mirror in BOTH this template and .claude/settings.json or test_template_dogfood_parity reddens.\",\n        \"matcher\": \"Bash\",","numLines":160,"startLine":1,"totalLines":980}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01KxHRKyctoF8e56jwg3cLXX","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
