{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012PX3j334DFjBvRbbSUUxX8","type":"tool_result","content":"334\t        ]\n335\t      },\n336\t      {\n337\t        \"_comment\": \"PLAN-124 WS-2 (ECC value-harvest) — adopter linter/formatter config protection. BLOCKING (maintainer ceremony). Allows first-time CREATION of a config (ENOENT) but BLOCKS any Edit/Write/MultiEdit that MODIFIES an EXISTING file in the UNAMBIGUOUS adopter-linter basename allowlist (eslint/prettier/biome/ruff/stylelint/markdownlint/shellcheck/tslint/flake8 — NOT pyproject.toml/setup.cfg/package.json, NOT governance configs which are the canonical guard's job per MF-L/debate K6). The insight: an agent 'fixes' a failing lint gate by relaxing the config instead of the code → 'fix the code, not the config'. Design choice = block-any-edit (ECC parity, revisitable; see module docstring). Escape hatches: CEO_CONFIG_PROTECTION=0 (session) or <repo>/.claude/.config-protection-disable (per-repo). User ceremony wires the ADVISORY variant (CEO_CONFIG_PROTECTION_ADVISORY=1 → allow + systemMessage steer, never blocks). Fail-OPEN on a hook bug; fail-CLOSED (bounded) only on a write tool with no resolvable file path. Raw tool input is never echoed (basename + resolved path only). MIT-attributed re-implementation of ECC scripts/hooks/config-protection.js.\",\n338\t        \"matcher\": \"Edit|Write|MultiEdit\",\n339\t        \"hooks\": [\n340\t          {\n341\t            \"type\": \"command\",\n342\t            \"command\": \"bash \\\"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/.claude/hooks/_python-hook.sh\\\" check_config_protection.py\",\n343\t            \"timeout\": 5,\n344\t            \"statusMessage\": \"Checking adopter config protection...\"\n345\t          }\n346\t        ]\n347\t      },\n348\t      {\n349\t        \"_comment\": \"PLAN-179 W2 US6 (ADR-195 work-boundary persistence) — ADVISORY ledger checkpoint, NEVER blocks. On a `git commit` that lands plan-scoped work (scope derived MECHANICALLY from the committed PATHS: any path under .claude/plans/PLAN-NNN/ or any path named in a plan AC — never from resolve_plan_id, whose session-coupling is the root cause PLAN-179 exists to fix), the hook reports whether that plan's LEDGER.md is in the SAME commit. PreToolUse is the only event where the omission is still curable (`git add <plan>/LEDGER.md` and re-issue) AND the only one whose output arm can carry `permissionDecision` — so the measure-first window and the FUTURE enforce flip measure the same code path. No branch in this module returns a decision today: there is no deny arm to disarm. Emits closed-enum ledger_checkpoint_recorded / ledger_checkpoint_skipped (SPEC v2.59) carrying identifiers and clamped counters only — never the commit message, the committed paths or the ledger content. Kill switches: CEO_LEDGER_CHECKPOINT=0 (rail off, and the skip is STILL measured so 'off' is observable), CEO_SOTA_DISABLE=1 (master precedence, fully silent).\",\n350\t        \"matcher\": \"Bash\",\n351\t        \"hooks\": [\n352\t          {\n353\t            \"type\": \"command\","}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"15f68acd-8563-46de-ac1c-c65891f7fb4e","uuid":"7944bc2f-0508-4cf7-9661-8354828b4027","timestamp":"2026-11-16T18:09:48.446Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.n5R3O9/tree/.claude/settings.json","content":"        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"_comment\": \"PLAN-124 WS-2 (ECC value-harvest) — adopter linter/formatter config protection. BLOCKING (maintainer ceremony). Allows first-time CREATION of a config (ENOENT) but BLOCKS any Edit/Write/MultiEdit that MODIFIES an EXISTING file in the UNAMBIGUOUS adopter-linter basename allowlist (eslint/prettier/biome/ruff/stylelint/markdownlint/shellcheck/tslint/flake8 — NOT pyproject.toml/setup.cfg/package.json, NOT governance configs which are the canonical guard's job per MF-L/debate K6). The insight: an agent 'fixes' a failing lint gate by relaxing the config instead of the code → 'fix the code, not the config'. Design choice = block-any-edit (ECC parity, revisitable; see module docstring). Escape hatches: CEO_CONFIG_PROTECTION=0 (session) or <repo>/.claude/.config-protection-disable (per-repo). User ceremony wires the ADVISORY variant (CEO_CONFIG_PROTECTION_ADVISORY=1 → allow + systemMessage steer, never blocks). Fail-OPEN on a hook bug; fail-CLOSED (bounded) only on a write tool with no resolvable file path. Raw tool input is never echoed (basename + resolved path only). MIT-attributed re-implementation of ECC scripts/hooks/config-protection.js.\",\n        \"matcher\": \"Edit|Write|MultiEdit\",\n        \"hooks\": [\n          {\n            \"type\": \"command\",\n            \"command\": \"bash \\\"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/.claude/hooks/_python-hook.sh\\\" check_config_protection.py\",\n            \"timeout\": 5,\n            \"statusMessage\": \"Checking adopter config protection...\"\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"_comment\": \"PLAN-179 W2 US6 (ADR-195 work-boundary persistence) — ADVISORY ledger checkpoint, NEVER blocks. On a `git commit` that lands plan-scoped work (scope derived MECHANICALLY from the committed PATHS: any path under .claude/plans/PLAN-NNN/ or any path named in a plan AC — never from resolve_plan_id, whose session-coupling is the root cause PLAN-179 exists to fix), the hook reports whether that plan's LEDGER.md is in the SAME commit. PreToolUse is the only event where the omission is still curable (`git add <plan>/LEDGER.md` and re-issue) AND the only one whose output arm can carry `permissionDecision` — so the measure-first window and the FUTURE enforce flip measure the same code path. No branch in this module returns a decision today: there is no deny arm to disarm. Emits closed-enum ledger_checkpoint_recorded / ledger_checkpoint_skipped (SPEC v2.59) carrying identifiers and clamped counters only — never the commit message, the committed paths or the ledger content. Kill switches: CEO_LEDGER_CHECKPOINT=0 (rail off, and the skip is STILL measured so 'off' is observable), CEO_SOTA_DISABLE=1 (master precedence, fully silent).\",\n        \"matcher\": \"Bash\",\n        \"hooks\": [\n          {\n            \"type\": \"command\",","numLines":20,"startLine":334,"totalLines":980}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_012PX3j334DFjBvRbbSUUxX8","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
